    "payload": {
      "content": "When reviewing the SIGN dimension for theoretical SSL papers, prioritize the broad research impact of reconciling distinct method families (e.g., asymmetric architectures vs. explicit regularization) and the practical domain impact of simplifying training pipelines (e.g., removing EMA). Critically assess the state-of-the-art improvement by checking if empirical validation is limited to small-scale datasets (CIFAR-10, STL-10) and small backbones (VGG11), which may not reflect real-world deployment scales. Note the typical absence of societal impact discussions in theoretical works as a neutral factor rather than a critical weakness, but ensure the core theoretical contribution offers a demonstrable advance in understanding.",
